# An operation as a mapping in one record, reached from other records through filters.
# Mul is exclusive or on 0 and 1: its text is the two inputs, and out is computed. Ab is the
# Mul whose inputs are the a and b of the Assoc around it, so 'ab.out' is a times b. A path has
# one dot, so Assoc names each product ('ab_out') before a filter reads it. A filter
# that reaches a record around it is decided once the whole text is read.
#
# An Assoc is eleven digits, with no newline at the end: a, b and c, then the inputs of ab, bc,
# (ab)c and a(bc). Exclusive or is associative, so every text whose products fit their filters
# is accepted (xor.txt); a product that does not fit is refused, naming its filter
# (xor_bc.txt, xor_ab_c.txt).
Element {Integer} value: 0..1
  1. {Digit}

Bit {0 | 1}

Mul {}
  left {Element}
  right {Element}
  out {Bit} from: left & right
    {0} if: left = 0 & right = 0
    {1} if: left = 0 & right = 1
    {1} if: left = 1 & right = 0
    {0} if: left = 1 & right = 1

Ab {Mul} if: left = Assoc.a & right = Assoc.b
Bc {Mul} if: left = Assoc.b & right = Assoc.c
Ab_C {Mul} if: left = Assoc.ab_out & right = Assoc.c
A_Bc {Mul} if: left = Assoc.a & right = Assoc.bc_out

Assoc {}
  a {Element}
  b {Element}
  c {Element}
  ab {Ab}
  bc {Bc}
  ab_out {Integer} calc: ab.out
  bc_out {Integer} calc: bc.out
  ab_c {Ab_C}
  a_bc {A_Bc}
  same {True} if: ab_c.out = a_bc.out
